  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mekong Sustainable Manufacturing Alliance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(China):  .The Mekong Sustainable Manufacturing Alliance activity will improve the competitiveness of the manufacturing sectors in the Mekong region through private sector partnerships and the application of robust environmental, social, and governance (ESG) safeguards and standards for manufacturers with operations in Mekong countries. FY 2021 funds will be used to promote private sector best practices that advance sustainable supply chains in order to minimize negative environmental impact on the local communities in the Mekong region, which, in many instances, is a result of PRC investments. The activity will work with brands in selected manufacturing sectors to increase their suppliers&apos; capacity to adopt standards and improve their ESG performance. It will also work to catalyze regional opportunities for improving ESG performance by creating a regional private sector network and engaging with industry associations to increase competitiveness in the manufacturing sector. Anticipated results include strengthened sustainability and competitiveness, increased regional knowledge of manufacturing sector ESG best practices and resources, and a more level playing field for U.S. companies, while creating more secure supply chains. This activity will promote sustainable economic growth in the Mekong region with a focus on the manufacturing sector. It will provide an opportunity for companies in Lower Mekong countries to enter the global supply chain if they are able to meet international standards. This will foster sustainable and secure supply chains and improved natural resource management. .</narrative>
  </description>
